course: dictionary
lesson: 7961
title: Who works at the front desk?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A receptionist is the person at the front desk of an office, hotel, school or doctor's surgery. They greet people, answer the phone and make appointments. When you meet a new word, read the words around it, because they are its context: «Go to the school office or receptionist if you are late, hurt or ill.» You go to a receptionist when you need help, so the word names someone who helps people who come in.
explain: Look for clues about the job. «Receptionists ask what the problem is so they can find the right appointment.» The clues are ask, problem and appointment, so a receptionist checks what is wrong and books a time to be seen. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? A shopkeeper or a footballer would not fit, so receptionist is the best choice.
explain: Phrases help too. You might hear «ask at reception» or a «hotel receptionist». Reception is the front desk or area where the receptionist works, so the two words are linked. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Receptionists take messages and phone families» still makes sense, so you have understood it.
fact: A receptionist works at the front desk of an office, hotel, school or doctor's surgery.
fact: «Receptionist» is a noun. One is a receptionist, and more than one are receptionists.
fact: Receptionists greet people, answer the phone and make appointments.
fact: «Reception» is the front desk or area where a receptionist works.
fact: In a school, the office staff or receptionist take messages and phone families when a child is late, hurt or ill.
exercise: «Receptionists ask what the problem is so they can find the right appointment.» Find and copy one word that means a time booked to see someone. | urgent | *appointment | problem | nurse
exercise: What does a receptionist do at a doctor's surgery? | Cuts hair and sells shoes | *Greets people and makes appointments | Teaches maths lessons | Drives the ambulance
exercise: What is a receptionist? | A doctor who gives medicine | A driver who takes people to hospital | A teacher who takes the register | *A person who works at the front desk, greeting people and answering the phone
test: Why might a child go to the school receptionist? | Because they want to borrow a football | Because lunch has finished | Because the head teacher has asked them to sing | *Because they are late, hurt, ill or need to phone home
test: Which word is the plural of receptionist? | *receptionists | receptionistes | receptionist's | receptionistings
exam: Where might you meet a receptionist? | At the bottom of the sea, fishing | *At a doctor's or hotel desk, greeting people and answering the phone | On a farm, milking cows | In a library, shelving books
